{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>to deliver, etc. and she puts forth her hand, etc.</b> Now the verse did not say ״and she puts forth her hand, etc. to deliver her husband״. By this it alerts us that if she had no way to save her husband from the hand of the one striking him except through this — because she has no power to save except by this means — she is exempt. And specifically where the other man was striking him a life-threatening blow; for this reason Scripture placed the phrase ״to deliver״ before the phrase ״and she puts forth,״ to say that if we know that she put forth her hand only to deliver — she is exempt."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:18:55.821285251Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}